  <!-- The testing model: the poster's six steps, in its order and nearly its words -->
  <section id="testing-model" class="section" aria-labelledby="testing-model-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="testing-model-h" class="h2 max-w-[44rem]">Six steps, from the sample to the follow-up</h2>
      <!-- [html-validate-disable-next no-redundant-role, prefer-native-element: preflight's list-style: none drops the list role in Safari/VoiceOver] -->
      <ol role="list" class="steps-numbered steps-text mt-12">
        <li><p><b class="run-in">Sample collection.</b> At a health centre, a school, an anganwadi or a maternity ward: a finger prick, a spot of blood on a card, and the details captured on the app.</p></li>
        <li><p><b class="run-in">Transport to a nearby testing centre.</b> Cards travel at room temperature, by ordinary courier or post. No cold chain, no ice box.</p></li>
        <li><p><b class="run-in">Molecular testing.</b> At the testing centre, many cards in one run, with no DNA extraction step.</p></li>
        <li><p><b class="run-in">Test reporting.</b> Results go back to the clinician and the programme. Affected, carrier or unaffected, each with a next step.</p></li>
        <li><p><b class="run-in">Patient management through proper treatment.</b> Genetic and social counselling for patients and for carriers, and a path to treatment where it exists.</p></li>
        <li><p><b class="run-in">Follow-up of patients.</b> Awareness programmes for the community, and patient support groups so that families are not alone with a diagnosis.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Before the test and after it: awareness and counselling, side by side -->
  <section id="before-and-after" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="awareness-h counselling-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="pair">
        <div id="awareness">
          <h2 id="awareness-h" class="h2">Before <span class="whitespace-nowrap">the test:</span> awareness</h2>
          <p>Awareness programmes explain inherited conditions and screening to communities: what the condition is, how it is passed on, who should be tested and what the test involves.</p>
          <p>Community screening and awareness camps are run together, so that a camp both explains and tests.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="counselling">
          <h2 id="counselling-h" class="h2">After the result: counselling</h2>
          <p>Counselling helps families understand a result and their carrier status, and what it means for treatment, for relatives and for the children they may have.</p>
          <p>For a couple who both carry a condition, it means knowing their options before the next pregnancy. For the family of a child with a muscle condition, it means knowing who else to test.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Support groups -->
  <section id="support-groups" class="section" aria-labelledby="support-groups-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="support-groups-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Patient support groups</h2>
        <p class="text-moss lg:col-span-5">A diagnosis is easier to live with among others who have one. We help set up patient support groups in the communities we screen, and work with patient organisations for the conditions we test for.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Where screening fits: four rows; the prenatal row waits for Part 8 item 29 -->
  <section id="where-screening-fits" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="fits-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="fits-h" class="h2 max-w-[44rem]">Where screening fits in a life</h2>
      <ul class="rows mt-10">
        <li>
          <h3>At birth</h3>
          <p>Newborn screening finds a condition before symptoms appear, so that treatment can start on time. Our tests for sickle cell anaemia and SMA can be run from birth.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>In the community</h3>
          <p>Population screening finds the carriers and the affected in a district, a school or a community where a condition runs.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>After a diagnosis in the family</h3>
          <p>Family and carrier screening shows which relatives carry the condition.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Before marriage or conception</h3>
          <p>Couples learn their carrier status before they plan a family.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Training, and help with setting up: side by side -->
  <section id="training-and-setting-up" class="section" aria-labelledby="training-h setting-up-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="pair">
        <div id="training">
          <h2 id="training-h" class="h2">Training the people who run the tests</h2>
          <p>We run hands-on workshops in molecular testing for laboratory staff and health workers, help laboratories set up the method, and advise on laboratory set-up and consultancy for hospitals and programmes.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="setting-up">
          <h2 id="setting-up-h" class="h2">Help with <span class="whitespace-nowrap">setting up</span> a programme</h2>
          <p>We advise hospitals and laboratories on setting up molecular diagnostics, support large screening programmes, and help with the planning of projects and grants: goals, budget, staffing, the laboratory and reviews of progress.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

