  <!-- From the field: three accounts, each in two paragraphs (R1) -->
  <section id="from-the-field" class="section" aria-labelledby="from-the-field-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="from-the-field-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">From the field</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Three accounts from our work with institutions. Details that could identify a family have been left out.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="accounts mt-12">
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">A diagnosis at three</h3>
          <div>
            <p>A three-year-old boy in a village in Madhya Pradesh was losing strength in his muscles. His family, a long way from any specialist hospital, took it for poor nutrition. An NGO working in the area arranged a molecular test, and the result was Duchenne muscular dystrophy.</p>
            <p>With a diagnosis at three, the family could begin supportive therapy and join a patient support group, instead of spending years without an answer.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Two carriers, one plan</h3>
          <div>
            <p>A couple in Chhattisgarh had lost their first child to spinal muscular atrophy without ever learning the cause. During their second pregnancy they were referred to us through a government screening programme. Carrier testing showed that both parents carry the SMA mutation.</p>
            <p>With counselling and early testing they could plan with full information. They now have a healthy child.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">What had been called fate</h3>
          <div>
            <p>In a village in Odisha, a young couple had watched two children in their extended family live with severe anaemia and repeated infections. Testing showed that both of them carry the sickle cell gene.</p>
            <p>In their village the illness had been put down to fate. The couple now know what it is, how it is passed on and what their choices are.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
